## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | IMPORTANT | scripts/sweep_stale_drafts.sh | ⚠️ important the fresh draft reclaim can delete a draft a still in flight train is about to publish train diagnosis selects the tag s newest concluded non success ci yml push run select conclusion success and conclusion null — in flight runs conclusion null are invisible to it that is correct for the stale path where the diagnosis only feeds issue prose gh 2105 the diagnosis is never a precondition but this pr makes the same output gate a delete in the fresh bucket and a newer in flight train on the tag changes which train owns the draft reproduced against the suite s own stub run status json completed fresh marked draft train runs json conclusion null … conclusion failure prov skipped sweeper deleted reclaimed early v1 0 750 … → x delete fired the single train shapes are safe only failed → intended reclaim only in flight → keep because the null conclusion alone empties the diagnosis but the mixed shape deletes a fresh draft while a live train may still publish it when that happens release provenance sign release checksums ci yml collect release assets starts with gh release download github ref name fails on the now missing release and the reclaim converts a recoverable in flight publish into a red train plus lost staged assets — the opposite of this pr s stated invariant never delete blind an in flight owner run keeps too the new test group s train still in flight case only covers the single train shape so the blind window is untested suggested fix small mirrors the in flight owner keep have train diagnosis also report whether any fetched run has conclusion null e g a 6th tsv field and keep the draft unless it is explicitly none — plus a multi train fixture null failure in the gh 2318 group pinning the keep the docs changelog fail safe keep lists would need the same one line addition |
| F2 | open | SUGGESTION | scripts/sweep_stale_drafts.sh | 💡 sugestion wrong issue id — gh 189 does not exist the rerun vessel convention is gh 189 this pr introduces the cross reference gh 189 in five new places scripts sweep stale drafts sh 29 keep list in the header scripts sweep stale drafts sh 67 train diagnosis header scripts sweep stale drafts sh 172 fresh bucket comment docs ci md 239 canonical ci doc changelog md 31 the new unreleased entry the convention being described — the staged draft stays as the rerun failed recovery vessel — is gh 189 scripts release draft dedupe sh scripts release train draft guard sh github workflows ci yml issue 190 gh 189 daily publish stale release drafts swept the same pr s test reasons use the correct gh 189 so the prose and its own tests disagree gh 189 matches no issue or commit in this repo s history this codebase leans on gh xxxx ids as institutional memory see agents md so these five point future readers agents at a dead reference one character fix ×5 the pre existing one off at test release hygiene test dart 337 gh 189 is untouched code here — worth fixing in a follow up not this pr |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

